To build your first colony, you need to be in a system that is within or connected to The Bubble by a chain, bridge, road, or highway of star system colonies. At any dockable location within that system, you can go to the Contacts Window, and find the Colony Contact. 

Speaking with them, you can begin a mission to claim your first/next system, provided it is within 15 Light Years. Making a claim requires 25 Million unrefundable Credits, and your ability to claim the system expires in 24 hours. If you had previous visited or scanned the system, known information about the system(s) will show up after a brief pause when you click on the green dot representing a claimable system.

The location of the Primary Port is denoted on the System Map by a flag icon, is pre-determined, and cannot be changed. It will be orbiting one of many kinds of different bodies, which help provide different economy overrides, and help boost or reduce the effectiveness of links. Once you select your system, you will be prompted to determine what kind of Primary Port you will want to build.

 Travel to the system and then the location indicated, then activate your System Colonisation Suite while you are facing and are within 750-2000 meters of the indicated position, and the Colonisation Beacon will deploy and within 3 minutes the Colony Ship will arrive.

The Colony Ship is not your new station, but it will “build” it for you if you sell them enough of the commodities it wants. Please note that the Colony Ship pays above the Galactic Average for these specific commodities.

Before we discuss the logistics, sourcing, and which specific commodities the Colony ships will want, we need to discuss how you should pick a system a little bit more.


